This repository contains the companion code for the HECKTOR 2026 challenge paper:

"Deep Learning-Based Segmentation and Feature-Based Clinical Prediction for Head and Neck Cancer"

The repository includes both:

1. Original code developed by the authors of this repository; and
2. Adapted components derived from the AdaMSS implementation described in:

Meng, M., Gu, B., Fulham, M., Song, S., Feng, D., Bi, L., & Kim, J.
Adaptive segmentation-to-survival learning for survival prediction from multi-modality medical images.
npj Precision Oncology, 8, 232 (2024).

The adapted AdaMSS components are included and redistributed with permission from the original authors. Copyright of the original AdaMSS implementation remains with its respective authors.

Permission is hereby granted to use, copy, modify, and redistribute this repository for non-commercial research and educational purposes, provided that:

1. Appropriate credit is given to this repository and the original AdaMSS publication.
2. This copyright notice and attribution are retained.
3. Any modifications are clearly indicated.
4. The original HECKTOR dataset and any associated clinical data are obtained only through the official challenge organizers and are not redistributed as part of this repository.

